      <pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/linux/troubleshooting_scenarios/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;30 Real-World Linux Troubleshooting Scenarios for DevOps Engineers&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;30-real-world-linux-troubleshooting-scenarios-for-devops-engineers&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#30-real-world-linux-troubleshooting-scenarios-for-devops-engineers&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When something breaks in production, you don&amp;rsquo;t have time to Google slowly. You need a mental checklist: &lt;em&gt;what&amp;rsquo;s the symptom, what usually causes it, how do I confirm it, and how do I fix it.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This guide walks through 30 of the most common incidents a DevOps engineer will face, explained in plain English with real commands. Each scenario follows the same format so it&amp;rsquo;s easy to memorize:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Linux File System Hierarchy Explained (For Beginners)</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/linux/ffle_system_hierarchy/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/linux/ffle_system_hierarchy/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Linux File System Hierarchy Explained (For Beginners)&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;linux-file-system-hierarchy-explained-for-beginners&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#linux-file-system-hierarchy-explained-for-beginners&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When you start using Linux, one of the first things that feels strange is the folder structure. There is no &lt;code&gt;C:\&lt;/code&gt; drive like Windows. Instead, everything starts from a single folder called &lt;code&gt;/&lt;/code&gt; (root).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this post, we will look at the most important folders in Linux, what they are used for, and simple examples so you can remember them easily.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Linux System Administration Commands: A Practical Guide</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/linux/linux_system_administration_commands/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 05 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/linux/linux_system_administration_commands/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Linux System Administration Commands: A Practical Guide&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;linux-system-administration-commands-a-practical-guide&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#linux-system-administration-commands-a-practical-guide&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As a system administrator or engineer, you deal with servers every day — checking what&amp;rsquo;s running, freeing up disk space, reading logs, or troubleshooting a network issue. This post covers the essential Linux commands you&amp;rsquo;ll actually use, grouped by task, with simple real-world examples.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;1. Process Management&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;1-process-management&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;span&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#1-process-management&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;These commands help you see what&amp;rsquo;s running on your server and control it.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
